@startuml locale
!include _theme.puml

title Locale — one preset, three parts you can move on their own

rectangle "Your preset\ne.g. Portugal — English" as preset #EAF3F8 {
  component "keyboard" as kb
  component "clock\n(Europe/Lisbon)" as clock
  component "language\n(English)" as lang
  component "formatting\n(Portuguese numbers, dates)" as fmt
}

component "Travelling to Zurich" as travel #FCF3E0

travel ..> clock : override just the clock\n(Europe/Zurich)

note bottom
  The preset sets all four together. When you
  travel you can change one part — the clock —
  and keep your language and number
  formatting. Coming home is removing that one
  override. `gisnix locale` does it for you.
end note
@enduml
